gpu_cached_indirect_buffers (on by default, hot reload): an indirect buffer executed again with the same address and
size is decoded once into the operations its packets perform (register runs, constant loads from memory, shader
loads, draws, nested indirect buffers, bin mask/select, event initiators, visibility queries) and replayed without
parsing while its dwords are unchanged (one memcmp against the copy taken at translation). Replays make the parse's
calls in the parse's order; register runs that already hold their values, where rewriting them changes nothing, are
skipped. Other type-3 packets (waits, events with memory writes, swaps) run their own handler from the buffer's dwords.
Buffers with a malformed packet are parsed as before, and buffers whose dwords keep changing are no longer
translated. Bypassed while gpu_draw_trace records. Counters in the gpu_frame_stats log, and a summary at each switch.

